# Race tests that use no seam, virtual time or simulator, judged: tools/check/race-tests.py says what a race test is and
# what each verdict means. <path> | <test> | <verdict> | <reason>. A race test that lets the scheduler pick the order it
# tests passes whichever way the race went; each entry says why this one does not depend on that.
kuicksilver-http3/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/webtransport/WebTransportServerSessionsTest.kt | negative_connectsRacingForTheLastSlotAdmitOne | not-a-race | asserts the set of outcomes (one admitted, one refused), which holds whichever CONNECT the server takes first
kuicksilver-http3/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/webtransport/WtDeadlineRaceTest.kt | negative_aBlockThatCompletesAfterTheDeadlineWasChosenKeepsItsResult | injected-hook | the session's wtTimer hook completes the timer only after the block started, and one thread (runBlocking) fixes the order of the resumptions
kuicksilver-http3/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/http3/webtransport/WtDeadlineRaceTest.kt | aBlockStillWaitingGivesNull | injected-hook | the wtTimer hook ends the deadline at once against a block that never completes: only the deadline can win
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientDnsTest.kt | theRaceAsksTheDnsOnce | not-a-race | the protocol race of RFC 8305 is the subject; one resolution is asserted whichever side wins
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientEventListenerTest.kt | aRaceReportsItsWinnerAndAnExistingConnectionIsReused | not-a-race | the protocol race of RFC 8305 is the subject; the events asserted follow the version that won, either one
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientEventListenerTest.kt | aDeadAlternativeReportsAltSvcRaceAndBrokenMark | not-a-race | the protocol race of RFC 8305 is the subject; the alternative is dead, so HTTP/1.1 wins every time
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientFallbackTest.kt | raceFailureMakesOneH1Attempt | not-a-race | the protocol race of RFC 8305 is the subject; both sides fail, and one TCP attempt is asserted either way
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientH2Test.kt | raceTcpSideIsH2 | not-a-race | the protocol race of RFC 8305 is the subject; UDP is silent, so the TCP side wins every time
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientRaceTest.kt | staleConnectionFromTheRaceIsRetried | not-a-race | the protocol race of RFC 8305 hands out a pooled connection; UDP is silent, so the TCP side wins every time
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientWebTransportTest.kt | negative_racingSessionsShareTheExtraConnections | not-a-race | ten sessions opened at once must share three connections in every interleaving; no outcome is waited for
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ConnectionPoolTest.kt | cancellationRacingReleaseNeverCountsTwice | not-a-race | a stress of 300 rounds whose counts must hold in every interleaving of the cancel and the release
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRaceTest.kt | hardDelayFromSrttClamped | not-a-race | a pure computation of the race's hard delay (RFC 8305 section 5); no concurrency
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRaceTest.kt | negative_hardDelayOutsideRfc8305BoundsIsRefused | not-a-race | a configuration check of the race's hard delay; no concurrency
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRaceTest.kt | negative_markEndsOnEitherClock | not-a-race | a broken mark on two given clocks; no concurrency
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRaceTest.kt | backoffDoublesTo2Days | not-a-race | a pure computation of the broken mark's backoff; no concurrency
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRaceTest.kt | markedPerOriginAndAlternative | not-a-race | bookkeeping of broken marks; no concurrency
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRaceTest.kt | workingResetsBackoff | not-a-race | bookkeeping of broken marks; no concurrency
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRaceTest.kt | negative_brokenMarksBounded | not-a-race | the bound of the broken marks table; no concurrency
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRaceTest.kt | markRemembersItsReason | not-a-race | bookkeeping of broken marks; no concurrency
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRaceTest.kt | networkChangeResets | not-a-race | bookkeeping of broken marks; no concurrency
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/QuicRaceFailureTest.kt | everyAddressRefusedIsARefusal | not-a-race | a pure function choosing the failure of the QUIC address race
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/QuicRaceFailureTest.kt | negative_oneAddressThatDidNotRefuseDecides | not-a-race | a pure function choosing the failure of the QUIC address race, in both orders
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/QuicRaceFailureTest.kt | aTimeoutCarriesEveryAttempt | not-a-race | a pure function adding the attempts to a timeout
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientDeadlineRaceTest.kt | negative_responseDataThatArrivedAsTheSocketTimeoutFiresIsRead | injected-hook | the channel's hook holds the read until the deadline cancelled it, and race() doubles the deadline until a run reached that point
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientDeadlineRaceTest.kt | negative_aWindowsPacAnswerThatCameAsTheBoundFiresIsTheAnswer | injected-hook | the bound's hook holds the answer until the bound cancelled it, and race() doubles the bound until a run reached that point
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/KeptWithinTest.kt | negative_anAnswerReturnedAsTheTimeoutFiresIsKept | retry-until-reached | the hook passed to keptWithin holds the answer until the timeout cancelled it; the timeout doubles until a run reached that point, and no run reaching it fails
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/ConnectionHandOverTest.kt | aResultMadeAsTheDeadlineFiresIsReleased | retry-until-reached | the block spins until its job is cancelled (the deadline fired); the deadline doubles until a run reached that point, and no run reaching it fails
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/h1/BodyDeadlineRaceTest.kt | negative_anH1BodyByteThatArrivedAsTheDeadlineFiresIsRead | injected-hook | the input's body hook holds the wait until the deadline cancelled it, and race() doubles the deadline until a run reached that point
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/h1/BodyDeadlineRaceTest.kt | negative_anH2BodyByteThatArrivedAsTheIdleDeadlineFiresIsRead | injected-hook | the input's body hook holds the wait until the deadline cancelled it, and race() doubles the deadline until a run reached that point
kuicksilver-native/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/native/KslLoaderTest.kt | negative_hashedCopyRaceUsesTheWinnersCopy | injected-hook | the replace function passed to installLibrary plays the other JVM that wins, every time
kuicksilver-quic/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/quic/core/PathTest.kt | negative_racedHandshakePacketDoesNotValidateTheSpoofedAddress | not-a-race | the sans-IO core driven by hand (HandPump): the attacker's copies arrive in the order the test writes, no concurrency
kuicksilver-quic/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/quic/NetworkMigratorConcurrencyTest.kt | closeRacingStartNeverLeavesItRunning | not-a-race | a stress of 1000 rounds behind a barrier whose assertion (the migrator ends) holds in every interleaving
kuicksilver-quic/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/quic/api/TokenStoreRaceTest.kt | negative_aTokenTakenAsTheDeadlineFiresIsUsed | injected-hook | the store passed in spins in take until the deadline cancelled it, and the next connection tries again when a run did not reach that point
kuicksilver-quic/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/quic/runtime/StreamObserverRaceTest.kt | firstReadersRacingTheLoopNeverLoseAValue | not-a-race | a seeded stress of 20000 rounds behind a barrier whose assertion (no value lost) holds in every interleaving
kuicksilver-tls/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/tls/CompletedWithinTest.kt | negative_aResultThatRacesTheDeadlineIsKept | retry-until-reached | the block spins until its job is cancelled (the deadline fired); the deadline doubles until a run reached that point, and no run reaching it fails
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientH3StallTest.kt | udpDroppedFromTheStartLosesTheRaceAtOnce | not-a-race | every datagram of the engine's QUIC socket is dropped, so the QUIC side can never complete: TCP wins whatever the timing
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRaceTest.kt | stallBackoffSurvivesAWorkingHandshake | not-a-race | BrokenAltSvc bookkeeping on the test's own clock: no concurrency at all
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ProtocolRaceTest.kt | negative_handshakeDoesNotLiftAStall | not-a-race | BrokenAltSvc bookkeeping on the test's own clock: no concurrency at all
